    "lawCode": "Add §§1221-a, 1221-b & 118-a, amd §161, V & T L; amd §22, Transp L; add §99-qq, St Fin L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S4647\n\nSPONSOR: KENNEDY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the vehicle and traffic law and the transportation law,\nin relation to work zone safety; and to amend the state finance law, in\nrelation to establishing the work zone safety fund\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill creates a penalty for endangerment of a highway worker, sets a\nfine structure, and directs sixty percent of fines collected to a work\nzone safety fund.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection One adds a new section 1221-a to the Vehicle and Traffic Law to\ncreate the crime of endangerment of a highway worker.\n\nSection two adds a new section 1221-b to the Vehicle and Traffic Law to\ncreate a public education and outreach program to increase motorist\nawareness about the importance of highway work zone safety.\n\nSection three amends section 161 of the Vehicle and Traffic Law to\ndefine a work area or work zone.\n\nSection four adds a new section 118-a of the Vehicle and Traffic Law to\ndefine a highway worker.\n\nSection five amends section 22 of the transportation law to clarify that\na representative of public employees must be involved in developing\nrules and regulations regarding work zone safety and enforcement.\n\nSection six creates the work zone safety fund. Section seven enacts the\neffective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nEvery day, highway workers face multiple threats from drivers, many of\nwhich drive around a work area, fails to obey traffic control, and\nendangers the well-being of highway workers. Further steps need to be\ntaken to punish these drivers, while deterring other motorists to the\ndangers they present while in work zones. By creating a new mandatory\nfine structure for violators of the law, people who endanger highway\nworkers will be held accountable, while directing funds into a new\nprogram to help prevent further accidents. These funds will be used to\nprovide work area safety enforcement, work area markings, radar speed\ndisplay signs, and police monitoring, so that drivers approaching work\nzones will properly slow down and yield to highway workers.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2021-22: Passed Senate\n\n2019-2020: Passed Senate\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nPositive impact to the state through the collection of additional fines.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect 90 days after it is signed into law.\n",
